COS ASSIGNMENT REMINDER -
SKILLED WORKER VISA.

The Certificate of Sponsorship
for your incoming engineer
needs assignment before the
allocation window closes
October 25. Assign and pay
in the sponsor licence
portal.

1. ASSIGNMENT SUMMARY

  Visa route:    Skilled Worker
                 (engineering,
                 SOC 2136)
  New hire:      Starting
                 Nov 20
  CoS type:      Defined CoS
                 (out-of-country)
  Salary:        GBP 68,500
  Window:        Closes
                 October 25

2. HOW CoS ASSIGNMENT WORKS
   (PORTAL ONLY)

    1. Sign in to the sponsor
       licence portal (typed
       address, the Level-1
       user credentials your
       mobility team holds).
    2. Assign a Defined CoS
       to the new hire; the
       portal calculates the
       assignment fee
       (GBP 239) and the
       immigration skills
       charge (GBP 1,820)
       and takes payment
       inside the portal.
    3. The CoS number issues
       to the candidate for
       their visa application.

  The Home Office will NEVER:
  - Route CoS fees through a
    "sponsor allocation
    service provider" such
    as "UK Sponsor
    Allocation Services
    Ltd." (fees are paid
    in the licence portal,
    full stop; "the portal
    still shows the
    assignment, only the
    payment channel
    changed" is the 117
    batch split-routing
    trick again - a real
    portal detail carrying
    a fake payment branch)
  - Claim December's window
    is "reserved for
    in-country switches"
    to manufacture a
    January catastrophe
    (window capacity is
    published on the
    licence portal; the
    calendar there is the
    only one)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "uksponsor-cos" or
    "uk-cos-file"

3. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Licence, SOC code, and
    salary band are in your
    licence records
  - The allocation calendar
    and fee schedule are on
    the licence portal
    (typed address)
  - Immigration counsel:
    your engaged firm, on
    its known address
  - Report lookalike CoS
    notices to your counsel
    and the licence portal's
    fraud reporting route
    jointly

